It now reads the **actual filesystem**, rather than displaying hard-coded fake folders. `Backspace` goes up a directory, `F5` refreshes, the mouse wheel scrolls, and opening a regular file delegates it to Windows via `ShellExecuteA`.

One architectural caveat: this is currently a **DirectX-backed shell UI with GDI drawing**, not a pure DirectX renderer. The natural next layer would be to move the rectangles, icons, text, hover states, and file list into a real **DX11 vertex/index-buffer + texture/font pipeline**, which would make the entire Explorer UI GPU-rendered.

