The heat map has **eight tiles**, one for each Australian state/territory. The colour is determined directly from `regional_score`, the number in each tile is the predicted score, and `#1`, `#2`, etc. show the ranking. The tile layout is only a visual state arrangement—it does **not** download or use roads, OSM, Overpass, or geographic map tiles.

Yes. I’d replace the previous version rather than keep patching it.

This version makes the model substantially more precise by using **state-level observations directly from ABS tables**, instead of multiplying the Australian national value by hand-written regional factors. It also separates **observed data** from **derived model quantities**, records the source period, calculates a transparent score, and reports each score contribution.

