### What this version actually does

Every execution downloads the current ABS pages rather than using the earlier invented example values. The current ABS dwelling release reports **$12.6889 trillion** of residential dwelling value and **11.5311 million dwellings** for June 2026. citeturn1view0

It then builds a regional dataset containing:

| Field | Source/meaning |
|---|---|
| `income` | ABS Average Weekly Earnings, annualised |
| `dwelling_value` | ABS dwelling-value data |
| `building_cost` | Derived from dwelling value + construction-price movement |
| `price_minimum` | Broad estimated range around regional value |
| `price_maximum` | Broad estimated range |
| `latitude/longitude` | Regional geographic reference |
| `source_location` | Regional source/reference point |
| `individual_id` | Numeric model identifier |
| `score` | Combined economic/spatial ranking |

The ABS earnings series is specifically published with state/territory data, and the May 2026 release was published in August 2026. citeturn0search9 The ABS PPI series includes construction and building-price measures, with the June 2026 release being the latest available as of September 15, 2026. citeturn1view2

**Important correction to the previous version:** the regional price factors in this code are explicitly labelled as **model estimates**, not real state observations. I would not want the program to quietly present fabricated state-level numbers as downloaded data. The next refinement would be to pull the actual state/territory rows from the ABS downloadable tables, so `NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`, etc. each use their own observed dwelling value and earnings rather than an adjustment factor.

Yes. Below is the **complete replacement project**. It is now **ABS-only**: no OSM, Overpass, roads, tiles, geographic downloads, or road-derived variables.

I also corrected the ABS approach: the program discovers and downloads official ABS `.xlsx` files from the release pages, then reads those workbooks with `openpyxl`/`pandas`. For example, the May 2026 AWE release provides separate state/territory XLSX tables, and Building Activity provides state/territory workbooks. citeturn0search0turn0search1 The June 2026 PPI release contains explicit state-level house-construction price changes, so the script uses that series rather than an arbitrary maximum value. citeturn0search2

