### What changed

The old program's entire OSM/Overpass branch is gone. There is **no `ROAD_TYPES`, `Overpass`, `adaptive()`, `bbox`, `tile`, `road_geometry()`, or road score** anywhere in this version.

The ABS flow is now:

```text
ABS release page
       ↓
discover official .xlsx links
       ↓
download/cache XLSX
       ↓
openpyxl + pandas
       ↓
identify exact state/territory series
       ↓
abs_data.json
       ↓
normalization
       ↓
16-sector golden economic vector
       ↓
golden similarity
       ↓
regional score
       ↓
predictions.csv / predictions.json
```

The PPI portion specifically uses the **House construction prices by state** series. The current June 2026 ABS release reports quarterly and annual state values, including NSW 2.0% quarterly / 4.8% annual, Victoria 0.7% / 3.7%, Queensland 3.1% / 8.0%, etc., rather than taking an arbitrary maximum from an Excel row. citeturn0search2

The AWE parser likewise targets the state/territory tables supplied by the May 2026 release instead of trying `read_html()` on the ABS page. citeturn0search0

