It can tell you:

- which transitions occur,
- how frequently they occur,
- how many possible outgoing transitions a token has,
- how dense the corpus transition structure is.

It cannot silently change the generator.

That keeps the graph useful for understanding the model without
turning it into a second inference algorithm.
