:::

### What the graph is doing

The important design choice is that the graph is **not another intelligence layer**.

For example, if the corpus contains:

```text
the cat sleeps
the cat eats
the dog sleeps
```

the graph is effectively:

```text
the ──→ cat
       ↓
       ...
cat ──→ sleeps
  └───→ eats

dog ──→ sleeps
```

Those edges come directly from the same observations used to construct the bigram/trigram tables.

So the architecture stays clean:

```text
                       ┌──────────────────────┐
                       │      CORPUS          │
                       └──────────┬───────────┘
                                  │
                    ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
                    ↓                           ↓
             N-GRAM COUNTS                 GRAPH COUNTS
                    │                           │
          ┌─────────┼─────────┐                 │
          ↓         ↓         ↓                 ↓
       TRIGRAM   BIGRAM    UNIGRAM        DIAGNOSTICS
          │         │         │
          └─────────┼─────────┘
                    ↓
